From f941edcef53a916e8aa5b3d2923af94a536cab1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 19:32:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DocumentsUI: give providers longer than 20s before declaring
 them wedged

Deleting a large folder from the microSD reported progress and then left
the folder in place. DocumentsUI hands ExternalStorageProvider a whole
subtree in a single deleteDocument call, and arms a 20 second watchdog on
every provider client. A 24k-entry tree on removable storage takes longer
than that honestly, so the watchdog reported it, AMS killed the provider
part way through the walk ("ContentProvider not responding"), and nothing
propagated back to the caller: files vanished, the folder survived, the
notification just stopped.

Raise the timeout to 10 minutes, long enough that only a genuinely stuck
provider trips it.

Deleting the tree client side instead (one call per document) was tried
first and reverted: it fixes the kill but runs at ~13 files/sec against
~870, because the per-document provider overhead stops being amortized
across the tree.

Changes:
- `DocumentsApplication`: `PROVIDER_ANR_TIMEOUT` 20s -> 10min, with the reasoning inline

Change-Id: I796011fa0f180fb86acd600e74d5f0b4bf2ac3ee
---
 src/com/android/documentsui/DocumentsApplication.java | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/com/android/documentsui/DocumentsApplication.java b/src/com/android/documentsui/DocumentsApplication.java
index c7e21a4..e8c4449 100644
--- a/src/com/android/documentsui/DocumentsApplication.java
+++ b/src/com/android/documentsui/DocumentsApplication.java
@@ -47,7 +47,13 @@ import java.util.List;
 
 public class DocumentsApplication extends Application {
     private static final String TAG = "DocumentsApplication";
-    private static final long PROVIDER_ANR_TIMEOUT = 20 * DateUtils.SECOND_IN_MILLIS;
+    // A provider is handed whole subtrees to delete or query in a single call, and on removable
+    // storage that legitimately runs for minutes: the microSD holds trees of tens of thousands of
+    // files, and 20 seconds of honest work looked exactly like a wedged provider. The watchdog
+    // then reported it, the framework killed ExternalStorageProvider part way through the walk,
+    // and the Files app showed a delete that progressed and then silently left the folder behind.
+    // Long enough that only a genuinely stuck provider trips it.
+    private static final long PROVIDER_ANR_TIMEOUT = 10 * DateUtils.MINUTE_IN_MILLIS;
 
     private static final List<String> PACKAGE_FILTER_ACTIONS = Lists.newArrayList(
             Intent.ACTION_PACKAGE_ADDED,
